  "description": "Alterations and extensions to roof to form front, side and rear dormers, with front and rear balconies.",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The development hereby permitted must be begun not later than the end of three years from the date of this permission.\r\n\r\nReason: In order to comply with the provisions of Section 91 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 (as amended).\r\n\r\n",
    "Condition : 2 - The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the following approved plans:\r\n\r\nPL 100, PL 107, PL 108,  PL 109,  PL 111,  PL 112, PL 113, PL 114,  PL 411, PL 412, PL 406 (Rev C), PL 407  (Rev C), PL 409 (Rev C), PL 110, PL 410 (Rev B), PL 404 (Rev E), PL 405 (Rev E), PL 408 (Rev C), Planning, Design, Access and Heritage Statement prepared by PPS, Fire Statement prepared by Joule Group.\r\n\r\nReason: For the avoidance of doubt and in the interest of proper planning.\r\n",
    "Condition : 3 - All new external work shall be carried out in materials that resemble, as closely as possible, in colour and texture those of the existing building, unless otherwise specified in the approved application. \r\n\r\nReason: To safeguard the appearance of the premises and the character of the immediate area in accordance with the requirements of policies D1 and D2 of the London Borough of Camden Local Plan 2017. \r\n",
    "Condition : 4 - Before the relevant part of the work is begun, specifications of external materials, and drawings as appropriate shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the local planning authority. The following details are required: \r\n\r\na) Full details and specifications of the materials proposed for the front, rear, and side dormers including cladding, window and door frames, and balustrades, with details of colour and finish; \r\n\r\nb) Details including sections (minimum scale 1:10) of the proposed windows and doors (including jambs, heads and cills).\r\n\r\nReason: To ensure that the external appearance of the building is satisfactory and that it preserves the character and appearance of the conservation area in accordance with policies D1 and D2 of the Camden Local Plan 2017.\r\n"
  ],
